---
import BaseLayout from '~/components/BaseLayout.astro';
import { SITE, VERSIONS } from '~/data/site';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Changelog — leptris"
  description="Releases of libleptris (the C core) and the leptris Ruby gem, with highlights and canonical changelog links."
>
  <section class="page-head">
    <div class="wrap">
      <p class="sec-label">Changelog</p>
      <h1 class="sec-title">Two components, <em>one core</em></h1>
      <p class="sec-lede">
        The C library and the Ruby gem release on their own cadence. This page
        carries the headlines; the repositories carry the full history.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="sec" style="padding-top:3rem">
    <div class="wrap prose" style="max-width:60rem">
      <h2>libleptris <span class="pill">v{VERSIONS.lib}</span></h2>
      <p><span class="pill gold">{VERSIONS.libDate}</span> — the C core.</p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Attribute handle iteration</strong> — <code>leptris_element_first_attribute</code>, <code>leptris_attribute_next</code>, <code>get_name</code>, <code>get_value</code>: O(n) enumeration where index accessors re-walk per call (O(n²)).</li>
        <li><strong>Mixed XPath nodesets, consumable publicly</strong> — <code>//a/@x</code> results no longer require internals.</li>
        <li><strong>Element prefixes</strong> — <code>leptris_element_prefix</code>.</li>
        <li><strong>External DTD subsets</strong> — <code>leptris_document_get_dtd</code> + <code>leptris_dtd_parse_external_subset</code>, with application-owned I/O; parameter entities and conditional sections work in them.</li>
        <li><strong>Public node-kind enum</strong> (<code>LeptrisNodeKind</code>) — bindings stop hard-coding numeric node types.</li>
        <li><strong>CI</strong> — a Windows DLL export check, and the FFI mirror drift gate.</li>
        <li><strong>Tooling</strong> — <code>scripts/gen-api-docs.sh</code> regenerates the Doxygen reference.</li>
      </ul>
      <p><a href={`${SITE.githubC}/blob/main/CHANGELOG.md`}>Full changelog in the repo →</a></p>

      <hr class="asterism" />

      <h2>leptris gem <span class="pill">v{VERSIONS.gem}</span></h2>
      <p><span class="pill gold">{VERSIONS.gemDate}</span> — the Ruby binding.</p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Precompiled platform gems</strong> (emf2svg-ruby model): <code>rake compile</code> vendors libleptris; <code>rake gem:native:&lt;platform&gt;</code> builds binary gems for x86_64/aarch64-linux (incl. musl, via Alpine containers), x64-mingw32/ucrt + aarch64-mingw-ucrt, and x86_64/arm64-darwin. <code>gem install leptris</code> works with no system libleptris and no env vars — the FFI search order prefers the vendored library. The pure-Ruby gem remains the fallback.</li>
        <li><strong><code>Element#prefix</code></strong> — the element&rsquo;s own namespace prefix (nil-safe).</li>
      </ul>
      <p><a href={`${SITE.githubRuby}/blob/main/CHANGELOG.md`}>Full changelog in leptris-ruby →</a></p>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
